[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2 Jelly Bean) port for the Huawei Y210. It is built on top of my CyanogenMod 9 port for this device: the same device tree work (RIL translation, Wi-Fi driver built from source, GPS, camera, hotspot) brought over to Jelly Bean, on a clean CyanogenMod 10 platform with only two small patches. The kernel is built from source.

[B]Device specs[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Device: Huawei Y210 (HUAWEI Y210-0151)
[*]Android version: 4.1.2 Jelly Bean (CyanogenMod 10)
[*]Kernel: Linux 2.6.38.6, built from source
[*]SoC: Qualcomm MSM7225A (the ARM9 modem runs separately and reserves part of the RAM)
[*]RAM: 256 MB physical, ~173 MB usable by Android
[*]GPU: Adreno 200
[*]Screen: 320x480 HVGA
[*]Wi-Fi: Atheros AR6003 (driver built from the AR6kSDK 3.1 sources)
[*]Bluetooth: Qualcomm Bahama (BlueZ)
[/LIST]

[B]Current status — Beta[/B]

Build: [B]PUT_ZIP_FILENAME_HERE[/B] | MD5: PUT_MD5_HERE

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read before flashing:[/B][/COLOR] please read the known issues. This is Jelly Bean on 256 MB of RAM: it works, but it is tighter than CM7 and CM9. [B]There is no FM radio and no GApps in this ROM.[/B]

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot & system:[/B] boots to the launcher after a clean flash; SurfaceFlinger, mediaserver and system_server stable
[*][B]Graphics:[/B] Adreno 200 for SurfaceFlinger and OpenGL ES 2.0 apps; GPU-accelerated UI drawing (hwui) is on and dialogs draw correctly
[*][B]Telephony:[/B] SIM, operator registration, signal and HSPA mobile data
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect (WPA2), DHCP; reconnects on its own after using the hotspot
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot:[/B] tested with two clients at the same time, browsing over mobile data
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] turns on and discovers nearby devices
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker and microphone (sound recording)
[*][B]Camera:[/B] preview and photo capture (1600x1200)
[*][B]Video:[/B] hardware H.264 decoder
[*][B]Accelerometer[/B] (the Y210 has no proximity or light sensor)
[*][B]GPS:[/B] the location engine connects to the modem and A-GPS runs over mobile data
[*][B]Storage:[/B] /data and SD card
[*][B]Memory:[/B] zram swap and Jelly Bean's own low-memory killer tuning
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]USB tethering:[/B] turning it on closes Settings. Use the Wi-Fi hotspot instead.
[*][B]No FM radio:[/B] same as CM9. Use the CM7 ROM if you need the radio.
[*][B]No GApps:[/B] a full GApps package does not fit in the ~186 MB system partition.
[*][B]Not tested yet on this build:[/B] voice calls and SMS (they work on CM9), SIM PIN, GPS outdoor fix, Bluetooth pairing/file transfer/audio, video recording. Reports are welcome.
[*][B]Powering on with the charger connected:[/B] a fix is included but not confirmed yet. If the phone stays on the boot logo, turn it on with the USB cable disconnected.
[*][B]RAM is tight:[/B] Email, the updater, DSP Manager and Voice Dialer can be disabled to free memory
[/LIST]

